      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Day 7 - useRef and React-hook-form:\nToday class i learnt implemention of useRef hook and\nreact-hook-form.\nuseRef: using useRef I handle the form. \nI created Form.jsx component for form impletation using \nuseRef and for display form data ui I\ncreated UseRefUI.jsx on form.jsx i used useRef hook\nand store data in setUser state\nlet formRef = useRef({});\n  let handleSubmit = (e) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    setUser(() => [formRef.current]);\n  };\n\nand for input i used like this.\n          ref={(e) => (formRef.current.productName = e)}\n\nand on user state I use map and pass object data\nthrough props inside the UseRefUI.jsx component.\n\nand rhf i created RHF.jsx component and use \nand install react-hook-from using npm i and \non rhf.jsx componet i wrote. \n\n  let {\n    register,\n    handleSubmit,\n    reset,\n    formState: { errors },\n  } = useForm();\n\nand on input i wrote \n{...register(\"proName\")}\n{...register(\"price\")}\n{...register(\"cat\")}\n{...register(\"img\")}\n\nand for storing form data I created function formSubmit\ninside formSubmit storing data inside setUser() function state. \n  let formSubmit = (e) => {\n    setUser(() => ({...e}))\n    // reset();\n  };\n\nand on displying data on ui I used RHFUI.jsx component. \n {user.map((user, ind) => (\n        <RHFUI key={ind} user={user} />\n      ))} */}\n\n",
